abstract: >-
  Glassbox is a local reasoning observability engine. Given a (prompt, response)
  pair from any LLM, it produces a structured, deterministic trace of the
  response: its claims, assumptions, contradictions, reasoning DAG, structural
  reliability scores per claim, and a battery of failure-mode signals. The
  verification core makes zero external API calls and is reproducible to four
  decimal places. Glassbox is the engineering substrate of the Glass Box
  Framework — a research program on visible, auditable, falsifiable AI
  reasoning.
